From 3244c12ac85f8a4b34a7136076ca3aee2d30ce6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GGEZUS <coelho.b.ricardo@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 20:20:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] feat(input): gesture debug logging behind gestures
 debug-log
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

First external bug report (NixOS): 4-finger gestures act as 3-finger
ones — the video shows all four touch points, so the compositor
receives every touch, but the 3-finger action runs. Not reproducible
on the maintainer's hardware, so diagnose remotely.

New `gestures { debug-log }` flag (off by default) turns on an
info-level event stream with a `gesture-debug:` prefix:

- every finger down/up/motion with slot id, position and timestamp
  (motion only while a sequence is underway, so single-finger app
  scrolling doesn't flood);
- phase transitions: entering recognizing, late finger joins, and the
  extra touch_down that arrives after recognition — currently only a
  trace line, invisible at the default log filter;
- recognition results (finger count, direction, hold vs quick) and the
  dispatch decision for taps, discrete swipes and edge swipes.

The flag lives on the tracker and is re-synced from the live config on
every touch event, so toggling it takes effect without a re-login.
Collection instructions in the README; no behavior change otherwise.
