 niri-config/src/gestures.rs          |  10 ++
 niri-config/src/lib.rs               |  18 +++
 src/input/mod.rs                     |  59 +++++++++-
 src/input/touch_swipe_tracker.rs     | 157 +++++++++++++++++++++++----
 src/niri.rs                          |   1 +
 6 files changed, 242 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Gestures.md b/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Gestures.md
index b42992b6..2d10729e 100644
--- a/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Gestures.md
+++ b/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Gestures.md
@@ -33,6 +33,8 @@ gestures {
         fingers 3
         // off
     }
+
+    // debug-log
 }
 ```
 
@@ -140,3 +142,21 @@ gestures {
     }
 }
 ```
+
+### `debug-log`
+
+Log touchscreen gesture events for debugging: every finger down/up/motion with slot ids, positions and timestamps, gesture recognition (finger count, direction, hold vs quick), and the action dispatched for taps, discrete swipes and edge swipes.
+
+The lines are prefixed `gesture-debug:` and written at info level, so they show up wherever niri's stderr goes (the journal for systemd sessions) without touching `RUST_LOG`. Off by default; the option can be toggled live, it takes effect on the next touch event.
+
+```kdl
+gestures {
+    debug-log
+}
+```
+
+To capture a reproduction:
+
+```bash
+journalctl --user -u niri.service --since -10m | grep gesture-debug
+```
